What was kept
-------------

* All original reader / parser / checker / writer / source modules.
* All original control-file keywords and their single-process semantics.
* The original SQL entry point shape, renamed to pgfastload.pg_fastload().
* The original COPYRIGHT file, unmodified.
* The original C file headers ("Copyright (c) ... NTT, Inc.").

What was added / changed
------------------------

* The project, extension, shared library, SQL schema, SQL function, control
  file and all build artifacts were renamed from pg_bulkload to pg_fastload.
* Version reset to 1.0.0 for the independent project.
* New control-file keywords PARALLEL and PARALLEL_WORKERS.
* TYPE=CSV, TYPE=BINARY and TYPE=FIXED with PARALLEL=ON now use multiple
  PostgreSQL background worker processes for stages (1)(2)(3); stage (4)
  stays serial.
* New modules: lib/fastload_parallel.c, lib/fastload_worker.c,
  include/fastload_parallel.h.
* Removed: an earlier experimental multi-threaded CSV prototype, together
  with its parser source file and build entry. The parallel implementation
  is exposed as plain TYPE=CSV / BINARY / FIXED, never as a new TYPE.
* New documentation (Chinese and English): README.md, README.en.md,
  docs/USER_MANUAL.md, docs/USER_MANUAL.en.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md,
  docs/ARCHITECTURE.en.md, docs/CHANGES.md, docs/BENCHMARK.md,
  docs/VERIFICATION.md, docs/OPTIMIZATION.md, docs/img/architecture*.svg.
  The inherited HTML manual has been removed: its numbers date from the
  PostgreSQL 9.3 era and its content is superseded by USER_MANUAL*.md.

See docs/CHANGES.md for the complete file-level modification list.
